ompleted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.4.beta1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev (24d74510e) - Fedora Linux 41 (KDE Plasma) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 (nvidia; 565.77) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K (32 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nA slow-moving RigidBody3D with a SphereShape fails to collide with a BoxShape that has its height set to 0 (essentially a quad collision shape). The RigidBody3D will fall straight through it as if the box didn't exist.\n\nIn contrast, it works when using GodotPhysics3D or against very thin CylinderShape3D (see below).\n\nThis may not be fixable on the Jolt side, so maybe it should just be worked around by disallowing the use of `0.0` in the BoxShape3D inspector and requiring it to be at least `0.001` like CylinderShape3D.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5c9b9ee3-1b9f-4da7-8365-83f7fc71b44e\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a StaticBody3D with a BoxShape3D that has its Y component set to `0.0`.\n- Add a RigidBody3D with a collision shape and make it fall on the BoxShape3D.\n- Notice how the rigid body collides properly as long as its speed is not too high.\n- Set the 3D physics engine to Jolt in the Project Settings and try again.\n- Notice how the rigid body now phases through the box.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test_box_thin.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18497769/test_box_thin.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users